{
  "id": "expedition-for-position-only-test-print",
  "name": "Expedition For Position Only test print",
  "category": "test",
  "description": {
    "text": "Test versions of Expedition's rares, made by Wizards of the Coast when it ran them through the printers before the set came out in September 2002. \"For Position Only\" is printed in white across the art and the word \"Medium\" in small black type at the bottom left, the e-Reader strip carries part of the e-Reader game Make a Dash!, and the copyright line credits Wizards rather than Nintendo.\n\nThe test cards went into unreleased five- and ten-card packs in Legendary Collection wrappers, for the design team only. A former Wizards employee saved the packs from the shredder and kept them for over a decade; they came to light in 2013, when most of the packs were opened on video. The Elite Fourum's guide counted 227 FPO cards by 2022, Charizard the most common of them.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: FPO (For Position Only) cards official guide",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/fpo-for-position-only-cards-official-guide/14586"
      },
      {
        "title": "WikiDex: For Position Only (TCG)",
        "url": "https://www.wikidex.net/wiki/For_Position_Only_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
